# Example Project — Project Context (Sentinel)

> This is a sample `project-context.md` for a typical Expo + Supabase mobile app.
> Copy this to your project root, rename to `project-context.md`, and edit the
> sections to match your actual data, roles, compliance posture, and risk surface.
> The MCP auto-loads this file on every audit pass.
>
> Last updated: 2026-01-15

---

## SENSITIVE_FIELDS

- `users.email` — GDPR/PII — never logged, never in analytics events, never in a URL
- `users.display_name` — PII — never logged, never in analytics events
- `users.phone` — PII — masked in UI, never logged, only collected with explicit consent
- `auth.access_token` — auth credential — SecureStore only, never AsyncStorage, never logged
- `auth.refresh_token` — auth credential — SecureStore only, never logged
- `supabase.anon_key` + `supabase.url` — credentials — env var only, never hardcoded
- `oauth.google_client_id` + Apple Sign-In credentials — credentials — env var only
- `analytics.event_payloads` — PII risk — scrub email and display_name before sending; hashed user_id only
- `sentry.error_context` — PII risk — scrub PII from breadcrumbs and error messages
- `push.device_token` — FCM/APNs token — never logged publicly

---

## USER_ROLES

- `user` — default, self-data access only (Row-Level Security enforced in Supabase)
- `admin` — full access to user data and audit logs. Web admin console only; no in-app surface yet.
- `support` — read-only access to user profile + session history. Web admin console only.

---

## COMPLIANCE_REQUIREMENTS

- GDPR — EU users have right to export and right to deletion; must be designed in from auth onwards
- CCPA — California users have right to know and right to delete
- Apple App Store Privacy Labels — must be completed before first TestFlight submission
- Google Play Data Safety Form — must be completed before first Play Console submission
- SOC 2 Type II — if selling to enterprise customers (deferred until first enterprise prospect)

---

## HIGH_RISK_FEATURES

- Auth flow — email/password, Google OAuth, Apple Sign-In, password reset (Supabase Auth)
- Supabase client initialization and Row-Level Security policies (RLS is the primary DB-level access control)
- `expo-secure-store` read/write patterns for session/refresh tokens
- Push notification device token registration (FCM + APNs)
- Deep links for password reset and email verification (Universal Links / App Links — NOT custom URL schemes)
- Third-party SDK integrations: PostHog (analytics), Sentry (error reporting)
- [DEFERRED] In-app purchases / subscriptions — re-scope before any payment code is written

